BT /F1 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 644 Tm (Enterprise helpdesks receive significant volumes of suspected phishing emails and SMS notifications.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 630 Tm (Conventional keyword filters degrade rapidly when attackers utilize unfamiliar wording or subtle cues.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 616 Tm (PhishShift is an educational decision-support triage tool designed to detect emerging social engineering threats.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 602 Tm (It features n-gram Jaccard template deduplication \(FR-01\), campaign-separated holdout splitting \(FR-03\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 588 Tm (and benchmarks Rules against TF-IDF Linear Classification and a Multi-Modal Random Forest \(FR-02\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 574 Tm (Testing confirms that while heuristic rules collapse to 46.8% accuracy on unseen holdout campaigns,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 560 Tm (machine learning models maintain 100% out-of-distribution holdout accuracy and 0.0% false-positive rate.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 0.10 0.20 0.45 rg 1 0 0 1 50 538 Tm (2 | Problem & Objectives) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 522 Tm (FR-01: Deduplicate near-identical templates prior to dataset partitioning.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 508 Tm (FR-02: Compare rule heuristics, TF-IDF linear classifier, and multi-modal tree ensemble.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 494 Tm (FR-03: Campaign-separated holdout testing to assess true out-of-distribution generalization.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 480 Tm (FR-04: Reject/abstain option under prediction uncertainty and safe explanation of risk cues.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 466 Tm (FR-05: Quantify false-positive rate on legitimate urgent messages and evaluate robustness drift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.10 0.10 0.10 rg 1 0 0 1 50 452 Tm (Exclusions: Inert handling only; no live URL fetching or code execution allowed \(NFR-01, NFR-02\).) Tj ET
